I know that I am slightly off-topic but I have a question regarding
to netfilter-based packet filters on SMP machines.

Maybe someone can hint me in the right direction.

Machine A: IBM xSeries 345, 2xXeon, Fedora Core 1, Kernel 2.4.22-1.21=
99.nptlsmp, e1000 nic
Machine B: IBM xSeries 346, 2xXeon, Fedora Core 3, Kernel 2.6.9-1.667=
smp, tg3 nic

Both machines show 4 CPUs.

The observed behaviour is the following:

Load is generated by having throughput of ~400Mbits (day-average) wit=
h
heavy connection-tracking (200k - 300k conntrack states).

Load on machine A is distributed over 2 CPUs,
load on machine B is tied to one CPU.
Hyperthreading is enabled on both.

Can someone hint me in the right direction
which tunable to set to get the 2.4 behaviour on 2.6?

Any hints (and redirections to other lists=B9) are welcome.

